  auto_audit_dates_legend: '**How to read dates (this is not just "yesterday/today"):**

    - **`mtime`** of `.sync/` markers — when the file was last written to disk.

    - **`content`** of the marker — time/date of the last *successful* operation (may
    be earlier than mtime).

    - **`health.log`**: left `[…]` — when the check ran; `sync=` / `charts=` / `finance=`
    inside the line — snapshot of markers at that moment (until the job updates the
    marker, the value "freezes" in time).

    - **Action logs** in §3: date in the filename — month of events; after the dash
    — file''s mtime on disk (old months often remain unchanged since vault migration).

    - Everything below — snapshot as of **"Generated"** in the header; regenerate
    after incidents (`obsidian_sync` step 5b.1 or `FORCE_SYSTEM_AUDIT=1`).'
